<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <!--
    HotPath.MqttBridge (C024 skeleton, C038 production form) — EMQX -> Redpanda `telemetry.raw`.

    Hold the E-08 shared subscriptions `$share/posGroup/veh/+/pos/live` and
    `$share/posReplayGroup/veh/+/pos/replay` — on two separate broker sessions, because the MQTT
    inflight window is per session and one session holding both filters would let a throttled
    backlog stall live delivery (R-09). Key each payload by the vehicleId in its topic, produce it
    to `telemetry.raw`, acknowledge only once the delivery report names a partition and an offset.
    It decodes nothing — normalisation, dedupe and anti-spoof are position-processor-svc's, and a
    bridge that parsed payloads would drop a sample it merely failed to understand.

    C038 adds: T-05's 20 samples/s/device backlog limit (Redis-backed, one lane per device, waits
    rather than drops), D-17's `mqtt.rate_violation` onto `audit.events` (the bridge reports it;
    EMQX's `messages_rate` enforces it), pipelined produces so a replica is not capped at one broker
    round trip per sample, and an unsubscribe-drain-disconnect stop so a rolling deploy cannot
    duplicate ingest.

    Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web rather than Worker: D7' §5.1 wants /health/live and /health/ready on
    every service, and readiness here has to answer for the broker connection, the Kafka producer
    and — as of C038 — Redis, where both rate counters live.

    NOT here: the LWT consumers (R-15/T-04 — trip-state, dispatch and fleet-health each consume
    `veh/+/status` themselves) and the `<topic>.dlq` (D6' §2.3, C039).

    Verify: dotnet test backend/src/HotPath.Tests -c Release, filtered to Category=MqttBridge.
    (The literal command is in this project's CLAUDE.md; an XML comment cannot carry a double
    hyphen, which is what a dotnet-test filter flag begins with.)
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MageRide.HotPath.MqttBridge</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MageRide.HotPath.MqttBridge</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <UserSecretsId>mageride-hotpath-mqtt-bridge</UserSecretsId>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\MageRide.Shared\MageRide.Shared.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Shared subscriptions and manual acknowledgement are both MQTT 5 features and both are
         load-bearing here — see MqttBridgeWorker. -->
    <PackageReference Include="MQTTnet" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="HotPath.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
